    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing now. Here's a summary of what I fixed:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Missing export in `src/finetune/index.js`**\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` directly, but it was only available through the default export\n- Kept the default export intact for backward compatibility\n\n**2. Incorrect function signature in `src/eval/metrics.js`**\n- Changed `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)`\n- The function was being called with `(outputs, references)` from `runEvaluations`, but expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)`\n- When references were passed as bannedTerms, the words in the references array got incorrectly flagged as \"toxic\", causing the score to be 0 instead of 1\n- Now uses `defaultBannedTerms` directly, which is the correct behavior based on the tests\n\n**Test Results:**\n- **8 test files passed** (was 6 failed)\n- **28 tests passed** (was 26 passed, 2 failed)\n- All public exports remain working and backward compatible",
